Escape sequence characters :-
\n :- endl
\t :- tab space

For a string titled str,
concatenation :- sum of two strings

Indexing is useful for accessing a specific character in a string str[0] is used. A string value cannot be manipulated using a str[0].

len(str) is a function that accesses the length i.e. no. of characters in a string.

slicing :- str[0 : len(str)] (excludes the last value)
str[start value : end value : jumps]
str[::2] (prints every two character)

iteration :- ch is used to find characters, 

a = yellow
for ch in a :
print(ch)

Output gives :-
y
e
l
l
o
w

string.capitalize() :- capitalizes the first character of string.

string.replace(“old val” : “new value”) :- replaced old value with a newer one.

string.find(“ch/word/string”) :- finds the letter/word/sentence/string

string.count(“ “) :- counts the no. of times that string occurs in the string.
